==Strategy==
A simple stage featuring Aliens and Zombies. All enemies in this stage spawn on a timer, so you don't have plenty of time to build up your team before the fight. It is highly recommended to bring high-damage-dealers like Can Can Cat to kill the first enemies as soon as possible. The main problem of the stage are Zollows and Nimoy Bores, so bring units like Catellite and Cadaver BearCat, along with other [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: It is a fact that Catellite can tank many hits from Aliens, and with its Weaken Immunity, it becomes a perfect candidate for this stage.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]: Due to the nature of the stage, it is better to bring units with high damage instead of high health. It will allow you to make money more easily and quickly.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Its high damage allows you to kill any enemies within seconds. In addition, if you happen to have its target Alien talent unlocked, the [[Slow|Slow ability]] increases her effectiveness in this stage especially against Nimoy Bore.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Her long-distance attacks will damage backliner enemies, and with her [[Zombie Killer]] ability, peons like Zollow will have less opportunities to hit your attackers. Also, having her [[Savage Blow]] talent helps.
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]: Their Anti-Zombie abilities make them able to clear all the Zombie peons, particularly good in using their Wave Attack to snipe Zollow before they hit you.

